[153.449362, "o", "QSIPrep does **not** have an `--output-spaces` flag (unlike fMRIPrep). The equivalent is split across two flags:\r\n\r\n| Flag | Purpose |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| `--anatomical-template` | Template space for registration (default: `MNI152NLin2009cAsym`, currently the only option) |\r\n| `--output-resolution` | Isotropic voxel size in mm for all outputs (required) |\r\n\r\n**Example invocation:**\r\n```bash\r\nqsiprep /bids /derivatives participant \\\r\n    --anatomical-template MNI152NLin2009cAsym \\\r\n    --output-resolution 1.25\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Caveats verified from the docs and GitHub:**\r\n- The anatomical template controls where the T1w is registered; DWI outputs normally remain in T1w space because T1w contrast is insufficient to align white matter to a template directly.\r\n- GitHub issue #681 tracks a planned replacement of these flags with a unified `--output-spaces` (fMRIPrep-style), but it is not implemented as of the current stable release (v1.1.1 / v26.0.0).\r\n\r\nChecked against: QSIPrep readthedocs stable usage page and GitHub PennLINC/qsiprep issue tracker.\r\n"]
[153.449763, "o", "\u001b[?1006l\u001b[?1003l\u001b[?1002l\u001b[?1000l\u001b(B\u000f\u001b[>4m\u001b[<u\u001b[?1004l\u001b[?2031l\u001b[?2004l\u001b[?25h\u001b7\u001b[r\u001b8"]
